<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Glückstadt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Glückstadt is a town on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, founded in 1617 by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-iv-of-denmark">Christian IV of Denmark</a> as a rival to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a>. Planned with a radial street pattern and strong fortifications, it became the seat of the royal Danish government of Holstein. Its harbour was later known for herring fishing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gluckstadt.jpg" alt="Glückstadt" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nightflyer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Glueckstadt,_Germany_-_Binnenhafen_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
